SUMMARY:Arsenic and Old Lace [Live Theatre]
DESCRIPTION:Drama critic Mortimer Brewster’s engagement announcement is upended when he discovers a corpse in his elderly aunts’ window seat. Mortimer rushes to tell Abby and Martha before they stumble upon the body themselves\, only to learn that the two old women aren’t just aware of the dead man in their parlor\, they killed him! Between his aunts’ penchant for poisoning wine\, a brother who thinks he’s Teddy Roosevelt\, and another brother using plastic surgery to hide from the police – not to mention Mortimer’s own hesitancy about marriage – it’ll be a miracle if Mortimer makes it to his wedding. Arsenic and Old Lace is a classic dark comedy about the only thing more deadly than poison: family. \n\nAbby Brewster: Becky Stapf\nMartha Brewster: Amy Frazer\nRev. Dr. Harper: Horace Tucker\nTeddy Brewster: Jerry Maguire\nOfficer Brophy: Mark Webber\nOfficer Klein: Devon Davis\nElaine Harper: Shaun Ancelet\nMortimer Brewster: Ben Sledge\nMr. Gibbs: Jackson Flora\nJonathan Brewster: Ben Bryant\nDr. Einstein: Steve Scott\nOfficer O’Hara: Robert Stevens\nLt. Rooney: Mark Owens\nMr. Witherspoon: Mike Harold\nUnderstudy: Harold Crooks\n\nDirector: Susan Rardin\nAsst. Director: Leslie Clauss\nStage Manager: Calla Imming\n\n\n\nBUY TICKETS - Friday Oct 2 - 7:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Saturday Oct 3 - 7:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Sunday Oct 4 - 2:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Friday Oct 9 - 7:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Saturday Oct 10 - 7:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Sunday Oct 11 - 2:30pm
